### Design Principles from Reference Sites

#### Camera Animation Standards
- **Smooth Easing:** All camera movements should use easeInOutCubic or similar smooth easing functions
- **Duration:** Transition animations should be between 1.5-2.5 seconds for perceived smoothness
- **Predictability:** Camera movements should feel natural and avoid jarring jumps
- **Context Preservation:** Camera should maintain spatial awareness and relationship to timeline

#### Timeline Presentation
- **Progressive Disclosure:** Show information gradually as user scrolls through timeline
- **Visual Hierarchy:** Use depth, scale, and positioning to create clear information hierarchy
- **Temporal Clarity:** Make it clear where users are in the timeline at all times
- **Navigation Feedback:** Provide clear visual feedback for timeline position and available content

#### Performance Standards
- **Frame Rate:** Target 60 FPS on desktop, minimum 30 FPS on mobile
- **Responsiveness:** UI should respond to interactions within 16ms (60fps threshold)
- **Resource Management:** Use lazy loading, progressive loading, and efficient memory management
- **Visual Polish:** Performance optimizations should never compromise visual quality when possible

## Three.js Human Language Mappings

### Camera Control Commands
- **"Move camera to frame X"** → `cameraController.moveToFrame(frameIndex)`
- **"Ease camera to position"** → `cameraController.easeToPosition(x, y, z, duration, easing)`
- **"Pan left/right"** → `cameraController.pan(direction, amount, duration)`
- **"Orbit around target"** → `cameraController.orbit(target, radius, angle, duration)`
- **"Focus on element"** → `cameraController.focusOn(element, offset, duration)`
- **"Play camera timeline step 3"** → `cameraController.playTimelineStep(3)`
- **"Smooth transition to scene"** → `cameraController.transitionToScene(sceneId, options)`
- **"Reset camera to default"** → `cameraController.resetToDefault()`
- **"Set camera FOV"** → `cameraController.setFOV(fov, duration)`
- **"Look at target"** → `cameraController.lookAt(x, y, z, duration)`
- **"Move camera to show timeline better"** → Ask: "Which part of the timeline? What angle would you prefer?"
- **"Make the animation smoother"** → Ask: "Which animation? What duration and easing would you like?"

### Scene Management Commands
- **"Add object to scene"** → `sceneManager.addObject(object, position, rotation, scale)`
- **"Remove object from scene"** → `sceneManager.removeObject(objectId)`
- **"Update object properties"** → `sceneManager.updateObject(objectId, properties)`
- **"Animate object"** → `sceneManager.animateObject(objectId, animationConfig)`
- **"Load image plane"** → `sceneManager.loadImagePlane(imageUrl, position, size)`
- **"Update timeline content"** → `timelineManager.updateContent(year, content)`
- **"Add a new image to 2015"** → `timelineManager.addImage(2015, imageData)`
- **"Adjust the lighting"** → Ask: "Which lights need adjustment? What mood are you trying to achieve?"

### Comment System Commands
- **"Add comment to 2015 event"** → `commentManager.addComment(2015, eventId, commentData)`
- **"Show comments for this event"** → `commentManager.showComments(eventId)`
- **"Hide comments"** → `commentManager.hideComments()`
- **"Edit comment"** → `commentManager.editComment(commentId, newContent)`
- **"Delete comment"** → `commentManager.deleteComment(commentId)`
- **"Reply to comment"** → `commentManager.replyToComment(commentId, replyData)`
- **"Like comment"** → `commentManager.likeComment(commentId)`
- **"Report comment"** → `commentManager.reportComment(commentId, reason)`
- **"Moderate comments"** → `commentManager.moderateComments(eventId)`
- **"Export comments"** → `commentManager.exportComments(eventId, format)`

### Animation Commands
- **"Play intro animation"** → `animationManager.playIntro()`
- **"Start timeline animation"** → `animationManager.startTimeline()`
- **"Pause all animations"** → `animationManager.pauseAll()`
- **"Resume animations"** → `animationManager.resumeAll()`
- **"Ease between keyframes"** → `animationManager.easeBetween(startFrame, endFrame, duration)`

## Debug UI Requirements

### Automatic Debug Controls
For every Three.js element added to the scene, automatically create debug controls with:
- **Range sliders from 1 to 10** for all numeric properties
- **Toggle switches** for boolean properties
- **Color pickers** for color properties
- **Dropdown selectors** for enum properties
- **Text inputs** for string properties
- **Performance monitors** for each object

### Debug Control Naming Convention
- Use descriptive names: `cameraPositionX`, `lightIntensity`, `materialOpacity`
- Group related controls in collapsible sections
- Include current values in labels: `"Camera X: 5.2"`
- Add reset buttons for each control group
- Include performance metrics: `"FPS: 60, Memory: 45MB"`

### Debug UI Structure
```javascript
// Enhanced debug control generation with 1-10 range
const debugControls = {
  camera: {
    position: { 
      x: { min: 1, max: 10, value: 5, step: 0.1, label: "Camera X" }, 
      y: { min: 1, max: 10, value: 5, step: 0.1, label: "Camera Y" }, 
      z: { min: 1, max: 10, value: 5, step: 0.1, label: "Camera Z" } 
    },
    rotation: { 
      x: { min: 1, max: 10, value: 5, step: 0.1, label: "Rotation X" }, 
      y: { min: 1, max: 10, value: 5, step: 0.1, label: "Rotation Y" }, 
      z: { min: 1, max: 10, value: 5, step: 0.1, label: "Rotation Z" } 
    },
    fov: { min: 1, max: 10, value: 5, step: 0.1, label: "FOV" }
  },
  effects: {
    spotlight: {
